  "prefLabel": "Plc 902.04 Authorized emergency aid training organization",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 902.04 “Authorized emergency aid training organization” means:\n\n(a) The American Heart Association, available at https://www.heart.org/;\n\n(b) The American Red Cross, available at https://www.redcross.org;\n\n(c) The National Safety Council, available at https://www.nsc.org;\n\n(d) The Emergency Care & Safety Institute, available at https://www.ecsinstitute.org/; or\n\n(e) Any other organization that offers a CPR or first aid course, as applicable, that meets or exceeds:\n\n(1) American Heart Association standards, for CPR certification; or\n\n(2) American Red Cross standards, for first aid certifications.\n\nSource. #14387, eff 10-17-25, EXPIRES: 10-17-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc900.html"
